# The optional Professions tab (brief PR3): its code and its compact data, in a load on demand
# folder of its own so a player who leaves the tab off loads none of it. ItemTree's stub
# (UI/ProfessionsStub.lua) registers the setting and the tab, and asks the client to load this
# folder at login when the setting is on, when the player turns it on, or on the tab's first show
# (Core/Modules.lua). Every file here registers into ItemTree's namespace through the global
# ItemTree, the way ItemTree_Data's modules do.
#
# The project ids above are ItemTree's own, so an addon manager reads this folder as part of the
# same project. X-WoWI-ID is deliberately absent: the packager takes the first value it finds in
# any TOC it reads, and ItemTree.toc leaves that line blank on purpose (docs/release.md).

Data\generated\Data.xml
Core\Professions.lua
Core\Craft.lua
# Brief OPT4: the small client helpers the tab's UI files share, before the first that takes them.
UI\Kit.lua
UI\Queue.lua
Module.lua
UI\Skin.lua
UI\Bar.lua
UI\Trainers.lua
UI\Layout.lua
# Brief TP1 (QA item 210): the tracked professions on the strip, read by UI\Pane.lua at draw time.
UI\Track.lua
UI\Pane.lua
# Brief UI15 (QA item 209): the "View in ItemTree" button on the client's profession window, built as
# this folder loads.
UI\WindowButton.lua
